This box plot illustrates the anti-rPA IgG antibody titers in mice immunized with recombinant protective antigen (rPA) alone or formulated with aluminum hydroxide (AH) or Nano-11 at various doses. It demonstrates that both Nano-11 and AH significantly enhance antibody responses compared to rPA alone, achieving similar titers at 200 µg and 50 µg doses. Crucially, Nano-11 maintains strong adjuvanticity even at a low dose of 12.5 µg, outperforming AH at the same low concentration, suggesting its superior immunopotentiation at lower doses.